### 1. Book under an id you own. Blocks ~30s while the slow tool "commits".
###    Kill the app during this window (request below). Restarting the app is what recovers the run;
###    re-send this exact request only to read back its answer, because the crash killed the
###    connection that was waiting for one.
###    Add "kill_after_seconds": 8 to the body and the app halts itself 8s in, so you
###    can skip the kill request below and run the demo in two terminals.
POST http://localhost:8080/crash/run
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "id": "trip-42",
    "reference": "ABC123"
}

### 2. Simulate a crash: SIGKILL the app while the booking above is in flight.
POST http://localhost:8080/crash/kill
